<title>GERMANY: Schaltbau takes over Kiepe Elektrik.</title>
<headline>Schaltbau takes over Kiepe Elektrik.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Munich-based Schaltbau AG said on Monday that it had taken over Kiepe Elektrik GmbH from Adtranz, itself a joint venture between Daimler-Benz AG and ABB.</p>
<p>Adtranz signed the sale contract with Schaltbau, which takes a majority stake, and a Bavarian government financing agency, which will retain a temporary minority holding.</p>
<p>Kiepe Elektrik employs 500 people in Duesseldorf and Vienna, Austria, and has an annual turnover of 200 million marks, Schaltbau said in a regulatory news release.</p>
<p>No price was given for the transaction.</p>
<p>Adtranz made the sale to meet European Union conditions linked to the merger of Daimler's and ABB's rail operations.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
